{
  "name": "414. MiniMax video v1 and v2 meet the contract (fork minimax video contract)",
  "description": "Pins TXE-6428 (contract C3, C4, C5, C6, C7, C9) for MiniMax video. Local fixture regression, no live provider calls: start tests/e2e/api/runners/provider-error-fixture.mjs, start an isolated gateway on tests/e2e/api/provider_config/provider-error-fixture.config.json and run with providerErrorFixture=1; every case is skipped otherwise. minimax_video is a custom provider on base_provider_type minimax with two keys (mmv-key-a, mmv-key-b) whose base URL is the fixture's /mmv, which answers with MiniMax's documented v1 and v2 responses and records every call at /__mmv. Row 2: a MiniMax-H3 create sends seconds, resolution, aspect_ratio (as ratio) and callback_url in MiniMax's v2 fields and merges extra.prompt_expansion_mode. Rows 3 to 9: out-of-range seconds, an inexact size, seed, audio and the three task control fields MiniMax does not take are refused with 400 caller_unsupported_parameter before any call; before the change seconds were clamped, size was rounded to the nearest tier and the others were dropped. Row 10: a succeeded v2 query returns usage (output_seconds, input_seconds, input_images, output_tokens), provider_status and a url video; before the change usage and provider_status were absent. Rows 11 and 12: a Hailuo 2.3 create goes to /v1/video_generation and its query retrieves the file, with expires_at one hour after the file; before the change v1 did not exist. Row 13: a v1 create answered with base_resp 1026 inside a 200 is a 400 carrying the code. Rows 14 to 17: cancel queries first and sends DELETE only for the queued task, with the key x-bf-api-key names; running and succeeded tasks and v1 tasks are 400 provider_cancel_unsupported. Row 18: the list reads /v2/query/video_generation. Row 19 reads the fixture's call log.",
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "414.1 reset the fixture's call log (fork minimax video contract)",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [],
        "url": "http://127.0.0.1:8791/__reset"
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "prerequest",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "if (pm.variables.get('providerErrorFixture') !== '1') {",
              "  pm.execution.skipRequest();",
              "}"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('the fixture reset its call log', function () {",
              "  pm.expect(pm.response.code, 'failed: ' + pm.response.text()).to.eql(200);",
              "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().data[0].reset).to.eql(true);",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
